{"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Polystyrene (\"Styrofoam\") is difficult to recycle, both because recycling facilities aren't commonplace and you can't make it into new high-quality polystyrene.", "category": "main", "reason": "main_content", "level": 2, "section_path": ["Did you know?"], "source_tag": "p", "source_type": "", "coords": "5,84.00,604.58,403.76,16.74;5,84.00,628.58,400.82,16.74;5,84.00,652.58,221.75,16.74", "warnings": [], "article_id": "article_17", "source_title": "article_17", "source_tei": "data\\articles\\extracted_grobid_tei\\article_17.grobid.tei.xml", "block_index": 10, "section_title": "Did you know?", "section_depth": 1, "word_count": 24, "text_characters": 160, "pages": [5]}
{"kind": "paragraph", "text": "In the US alone, it is estimated that the annual volume of plastic waste produced is over 42 million metric tons, only 8.7% of which is recycled. About a third of all the food produced globally is never eaten. If we stop wasting food, we can reduce around 6%-8% of all human-caused greenhouse gas emissions. With some planning and small steps in preparation, storage, and freezing, you can make great strides to decrease waste in your kitchen at home and save money, too.", "category": "main", "reason": "main_content", "level": 2, "section_path": ["Did you know?"], "source_tag": "p", "source_type": "", "coords": "5,84.00,684.08,422.56,16.74;5,84.00,708.08,390.09,16.74;5,84.00,732.08,117.54,16.74;5,84.00,763.58,415.92,16.74;6,84.00,39.68,385.09,16.74;6,84.00,63.68,421.81,16.74;6,84.00,87.68,410.11,16.74;6,84.00,111.68,408.40,16.74;6,84.00,135.68,142.27,16.74", "warnings": [], "article_id": "article_17", "source_title": "article_17", "source_tei": "data\\articles\\extracted_grobid_tei\\article_17.grobid.tei.xml", "block_index": 11, "section_title": "Did you know?", "section_depth": 1, "word_count": 86, "text_characters": 471, "pages": [5, 6]}
{"kind": "paragraph", "text": "In the US alone, producing food we lose or waste generates the equivalent of 32.6 million cars' worth of greenhouse gas emissions. If you've got some small outdoor space, consider starting a compost bin, or see if there are community options nearby to drop off your inedible scraps or peelings.", "category": "main", "reason": "main_content", "level": 2, "section_path": ["Did you know?"], "source_tag": "p", "source_type": "", "coords": "6,84.00,167.18,422.59,16.74;6,84.00,191.18,370.08,16.74;6,84.00,215.18,400.05,16.74;6,84.00,239.18,401.72,16.74;6,84.00,263.18,336.50,16.74", "warnings": [], "article_id": "article_17", "source_title": "article_17", "source_tei": "data\\articles\\extracted_grobid_tei\\article_17.grobid.tei.xml", "block_index": 12, "section_title": "Did you know?", "section_depth": 1, "word_count": 52, "text_characters": 294, "pages": [6]}
